# Image Slider

A custom image slider built with vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No libraries or carousel plugins.

**Live demo:** https://d1ps0n.github.io/Image-Slider/

## Features

- Previous and Next arrow buttons on the left and right edges of the viewing window
- Dynamically generated indicator dots that update with the active slide
- Clickable dots that jump straight to any image
- Smooth horizontal sliding using `transform: translateX()` and CSS `transition`
- Seamless looping in both directions (Next on the last slide and Previous on the first)
- Responsive layout that scales with the container and screen size
- Images keep their aspect ratio with `object-fit: cover`
- Keyboard support with the left and right arrow keys

## Project structure

```
Image-Slider/
├── index.html    # Slider markup and sample images
├── style.css     # Layout, sliding track, controls, responsive rules
├── slider.js     # ImageSlider class: indexing, events, loop logic
└── Images/       # Sample photos
```

## How it works

- The slides sit in a flex track inside a viewport with `overflow: hidden`, and the track moves with `translateX()`.
- JavaScript adds a clone of the last slide at the start and a clone of the first slide at the end. After the animation lands on a clone, the track snaps to the matching real slide with no transition, which creates the endless loop.
- Clicks that arrive during an animation are queued, so fast clicking doesn't break the slider.

## Run locally

1. Download or clone the repository.
2. Open `index.html` in a browser.

